# Security notice: {{ .Case.Title }}

Tell the users affected, and where appropriate all users, about the {{ if .IsIncident }}incident{{ else }}vulnerability{{ end }} and what they can do
(CRA Article 14(8)). This runs in parallel with the reports: do it as soon as you can, not after the final report.

- Tell the affected users first, where they will see it: in the product, by e-mail.
- Before a fix exists, say what users should do, not how the flaw works. Details can help attackers.
- Publish the full details once the security update is out (Annex I Part II(4)).
- Where appropriate, also give it in a structured, machine-readable form (Article 14(8)):
  `shipward report drafts {{ .ID }} --csaf` writes this notice as a CSAF 2.0 document (`users.csaf.json`, a draft
  to check). For a flaw in a component, a VEX decision can help too (`shipward triage set`, `shipward triage export`).

Then run `shipward report done {{ .ID }} users`.

